<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from open market operations on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Analysts had weighed in on the side of no action but with Federal funds trading at a soft 5.00 percent, they cited a chance that the Fed would drain reserves from the banking system.</p>
<p>The Fed's target for the Fed funds rate is currently 5-1/4 percent.</p>
<p>-- North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679</p>
